If we named it `RunAndExit(command)` I could buy that.  Or if you want to be paranoid:

If you Exit() in here, the defer() will not get called - you'd have to next it.

```
// Should never return
func Run(command) {
    os.Exit(reallyRun(command))
}

fun reallyRun(command) int {
    defer(...)
    // all this good stuff...
}
```
